    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 64 An Fiodán is brought to the market For Sale by Private Treaty. This impressive four-bedroom semi-detached residence is ideally positioned within a well-maintained and highly regarded development, enjoying a peaceful setting in a quiet cul-de-sac.\n\nBright and spacious accommodation extends throughout and comprises an inviting entrance hall, a welcoming living room featuring a large bay window, a well-appointed kitchen/dining area, and a guest WC on the ground floor. Upstairs, there are four generously sized bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with en-suite, together with a hot press and a main family bathroom. Externally, the property benefits from off-street parking to the front and gated side access leading to the rear garden.\n\nAn Fiodán is a highly sought-after residential location, conveniently situated within walking distance of both primary and secondary schools, Lidl, Briarhill Shopping Centre, local playgrounds, and a soccer pitch. The development is also just 6km from Galway City Centre and enjoys excellent connectivity to Parkmore and Ballybane Industrial Estates, as well as the M6 motorway network.\n\nThis superb home will appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, families, and investors alike. Early viewing is highly recommended and is guaranteed not to disappoint."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nLaminate wooden floor, side aspect window, under stairs storage, coving.\n\nLiving Room: - \nLaminate wooden floor, large front aspect window overlooking communal area, coving, wooden fireplace with gas fire inset, double doors to kitchen/dining room.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: - \nSpacious room to the rear of the property. Laminate wooden floor in the dining room area with french doors leading to the private rear garden. Tiled floor in kitchen with fully fitted kitchen units, electric cooker and hob, plumbed for dishwasher, rear aspect window.\n\nWC: - \nTiled floor, wc, wash hand basin, side aspect window.\n\nLanding: - \nCarpet stairs lead to first floor, laminate wooden floor on landing, side aspect window, access to attic.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nSpacious double room with laminate wooden floor, large front aspect window, fitted wardrobes.\n\nEn-Suite: - \nRefurbished en-suite, fully tiled, wc, wash hand basin, shower, heated towel rail, extractor fan.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nNewly fitted carpet, front aspect window, fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom: - \nRecently furbished bathroom, fully tiled, wc, wash hand basin, shower unit, heated towel rail, extractor fan.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nCarpet floor, rear aspect window, fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nLaminate wooden floor, rear aspect window.\n\nHotpress: - \nShelved hotpress.\n\nGarden: - \nRear garden laid in lawn with block wall boundary, ideal space for outdoor dining and entertaining, gated side access. Off street parking to the front.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Gas fired central heating</li><li>Refurbished bathroom and en-suite</li><li>Upgraded gas boiler</li><li>New flooring</li><li>Excellent location</li><li>Management Fee 325 per annum approx.</ul>"
      },
